! ===========================================================================
!  ansys_ff_oop_halfsector.inp  --  Mechanical APDL batch deck
!  HALF-SECTOR PARITY CLASSIFICATION of the free-free FF-P1 FE modes.
!
!  WHY (addendum 2026-07-11 Sec I; LESSONS_LEARNED Sec 10.7 item 8, never
!  executed until now): the OOP ceiling item -- solver dip raw=2.828013
!  (Omega_lit ~= 111.65) vs the one unmatched FE mode Omega_lit = 111.4627
!  -- exhausted three genuinely different Python-side techniques (basis
!  bump, sensitivity map, null-vector gap; jobs 2316969/2317010/2317114)
!  without resolution, and Sec I explicitly names ONE genuinely new lever:
!  classify the FE mode's PARITY about the sector bisector independently,
!  sidestepping the rM/gap circularity entirely. The free-free wave
!  solution's K is block-diagonal in parity (post-B12), so every solver
!  dip lives in a definite parity block. If the FE 111.4627 mode's parity
!  matches the block hosting the 2.828013 dip, that is independent
!  evidence FOR the match; if it is the OTHER parity, the documented
!  model-vs-FE gap is confirmed structurally (the solver's candidate
!  cannot be that FE mode at all).
!
!  METHOD: model HALF the sector (0..45 deg; full sector is 0..90, bisector
!  at 45) with the identical SHELL281 setup as ansys_ff_oop_ext.inp, all
!  outer edges free, and the cut edge at theta=45 given (pass S) SYMMETRY
!  or (pass A) ANTISYMMETRY conditions about the bisector r-z plane. In
!  cylindrical nodal coordinates (x=radial, y=hoop, z=axial):
!     SYMM: UY=0, ROTX=0, ROTZ=0   (DSYM,SYMM,Y,11)
!     ANTI: UX=0, UZ=0,  ROTY=0    (DSYM,ASYM,Y,11)
!  Each full-sector FFFF elastic mode appears in EXACTLY ONE of the two
!  passes at (mesh-convergence-level) the same frequency: SYMM pass = EVEN
!  parity, ANTI pass = ODD parity. Two mesh passes per BC for the
!  convergence gate (radial 64 / arc 32, then radial 96 / arc 48 --
!  element sizes matched to the full-sector mesh64/mesh96 runs).
!
!  GEOMETRY/MATERIAL (identical to ansys_ff_oop_ext.inp): R_i=4, R_o=8,
!  half-angle 45 deg, H=0.08, E=210e9, nu=0.30, rho=7800.
!  Omega_lit = w*R_o^2*sqrt(rho*H/D), D=E*H^3/(12(1-nu^2)).
!
!  MODE-FAMILY SEPARATION: as in ansys_ff_oop_ext.inp -- discard any mode
!  whose f[Hz] matches the PLANE183 pure-IP list (ip_modes_mesh80.txt, job
!  2316743) within ~0.5%; discard ~0 Hz rigid modes; the remainder are OOP.
!  (The IP modes also split cleanly by parity, so the SYMM/ANTI lists
!  together should reproduce the full-sector inventory -- a free
!  completeness check.)
!
!  PRE-REGISTERED READING (do not reinterpret after the fact):
!    0. CONVERGENCE GATE: per-BC, mesh64-equiv vs mesh96-equiv elastic
!       modes must agree <0.3% before anything else is read.
!    1. CALIBRATION GATE: the four FE OOP modes whose solver-side parity
!       is already known (Sec 10.6 item H) must classify as:
!           15.128 (mode 2)  -> EVEN  (SYMM pass)
!           24.190 (mode 3)  -> ODD   (ANTI pass)
!           37.818 (mode 5)  -> ODD   (ANTI pass)
!           53.828 (mode 7)  -> EVEN  (SYMM pass)
!       If ANY of the four mismatches, the SYMM/ANTI<->parity convention
!       mapping (or the deck itself) is wrong -- STOP, do not read item 2.
!       (If all four land consistently INVERTED, the labels are swapped:
!       fix the mapping, then proceed -- still a pass.)
!    2. DECISIVE READ: which pass contains Omega_lit ~= 111.46?
!       Its parity is the FE mode's parity. Compare NEXT SESSION against
!       the parity block hosting the solver's raw=2.828013 dip (read from
!       job 2317114's gap-diagnostic output, which records sig_this's
!       block, or one cheap solver call):
!         same parity  -> the 0.16% proximity match becomes plausible
!                         again; a targeted re-adjudication with the
!                         parity constraint in hand is justified.
!         other parity -> the model-vs-FE gap is confirmed structurally;
!                         the item stays CLOSED as documented (Sec I).
!    3. BONUS INVENTORY: full parity table for every OOP mode up to
!       ~Omega_lit 120 -- external hardening for the entire FF-P1 table
!       (Sec 10.7 item 8), archived for future window extensions.
!
!  Run headless:
!    mapdl -b -i ansys_ff_oop_halfsector.inp -o ansys_ff_oop_halfsector_out.txt
!  Outputs: oop_hs_symm_mesh64.txt, oop_hs_symm_mesh96.txt,
!           oop_hs_anti_mesh64.txt, oop_hs_anti_mesh96.txt
! ===========================================================================

! ======================= PASS S1: SYMM, mesh64-equiv =======================
FINISH
/CLEAR,NOSTART
/TITLE, half-sector FFFF -- SYMM bisector BC, mesh64-equiv

R_i    = 4.0
R_o    = 8.0
PHI_H  = 45.0
H      = 0.08
E_iso  = 210.0e9
NU_iso = 0.30
RHO    = 7800.0
NDIVR  = 64
NDIVA  = 32
NMODES = 40
PI     = 3.14159265358979

/PREP7
LOCAL, 11, 1, 0,0,0
CSYS, 11
ET, 1, SHELL281
SECTYPE, 1, SHELL
SECDATA, H, 1
MP, EX,1,E_iso $ MP, EY,1,E_iso $ MP, EZ,1,E_iso
MP, PRXY,1,NU_iso $ MP, PRYZ,1,NU_iso $ MP, PRXZ,1,NU_iso
GG = E_iso/(2*(1+NU_iso))
MP, GXY,1,GG $ MP, GYZ,1,GG $ MP, GXZ,1,GG
MP, DENS,1,RHO
CSYS, 0
PCIRC, R_i, R_o, 0, PHI_H
ESYS, 11
TYPE,1 $ SECNUM,1 $ MAT,1
CSYS, 11
LSEL, S, LOC, Y, 0  $ LSEL, A, LOC, Y, PHI_H
LESIZE, ALL, , , NDIVA
LSEL, S, LOC, X, R_i $ LSEL, A, LOC, X, R_o
LESIZE, ALL, , , NDIVR
ALLSEL, ALL
CSYS, 0
MSHKEY, 1 $ AMESH, ALL
! bisector cut edge (theta = PHI_H): rotate nodes to cylindrical, SYMM set
CSYS, 11
NSEL, S, LOC, Y, PHI_H
NROTAT, ALL
DSYM, SYMM, Y, 11        ! = D UY,ROTX,ROTZ = 0 in cylindrical nodal coords
ALLSEL, ALL
CSYS, 0
FINISH

/SOLU
ANTYPE, MODAL
MODOPT, LANB, NMODES, -1.0, , , ON
MXPAND, NMODES, , , YES
SOLVE
FINISH

/POST1
DD   = E_iso*H**3/(12*(1-NU_iso**2))
KLIT = R_o**2*SQRT(RHO*H/DD)
*DIM, FRS1, ARRAY, NMODES
*DO, I, 1, NMODES
  *GET, FRS1(I), MODE, I, FREQ
*ENDDO
*CFOPEN, oop_hs_symm_mesh64, txt
*VWRITE
('mode      f[Hz]           Omega_lit    (half-sector SYMM=EVEN parity; SHELL281 r64/a32; discard ~0Hz rigid + IP-matching modes)')
*DO, I, 1, NMODES
  OML = 2*PI*FRS1(I)*KLIT
  *VWRITE, I, FRS1(I), OML
(F4.0, 3X, E14.6, 3X, F12.4)
*ENDDO
*CFCLOS
FINISH

! ======================= PASS S2: SYMM, mesh96-equiv =======================
FINISH
/CLEAR,NOSTART
/TITLE, half-sector FFFF -- SYMM bisector BC, mesh96-equiv

R_i    = 4.0
R_o    = 8.0
